  <description><![CDATA[ Stories of might and main, romance and tragedy among the Tuatha DeDanaan with Brigit, Lir, Manannaun, Ethaun and others. Great ancient gods of wind, water and earth and their children mingle with people of the Faeries, heroes and the after-world. Told with poetry and wit by Ella Young in an old and familiar 'honey-sweet wisdom of speech'. An important part of the Celtic revival in Ireland.- Summary by Czandra]]></description>
